        <div class="protocol__glyph" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" fill="none">
            <path d="M20 6 C12.3 6 6 12.1 6 19.6 c0 2.8.9 5.4 2.5 7.5 L7 34 l7.2-1.9 c1.8.9 3.8 1.3 5.8 1.3 7.7 0 14-6.1 14-13.8S27.7 6 20 6Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            <path d="M15 13.5 c-.5-.8-1.2-.7-1.7-.2-.8.8-1.3 1.7-1.1 2.8.4 3.6 4.8 8.1 8.4 9.1 1.1.3 2.1-.1 2.9-.8.6-.5.9-1.2.4-1.7l-2.3-1.7c-.5-.3-.9-.2-1.3.3l-.8 1c-1.9-.8-3.4-2.2-4.3-4l.9-.9c.4-.4.5-.8.2-1.3l-1.3-2.6Z" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="protocol__name">WhatsApp</h2>
          <p class="protocol__sub">Outgoing text messages through the WhatsApp Business Cloud API.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="protocol__link" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sockethub/platform-whatsapp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          @sockethub/platform-whatsapp ↗
        </a>
        <span class="protocol__badge">New in 5.0</span>
      </header>

      <div class="protocol__body">
        <p>
          Send text messages from a WhatsApp Business phone number using
          Meta's Cloud API. The platform is stateless: set credentials, then
          send. Incoming messages and recipient discovery stay in your own
          Meta webhook integration.
        </p>

        <p class="protocol__flow-note">
          The full WhatsApp flow is <strong>credentials → send</strong>.
          Sockethub does not host webhooks or run OAuth; your app obtains and
          supplies the access token.
        </p>

        <h3 class="protocol__section">1. Credentials</h3>
        <pre class="envelope-block"><code>{
  <span class="tok-key">"@context"</span>: [
    <span class="tok-str">"https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams"</span>,
    <span class="tok-str">"https://sockethub.org/ns/context/v1.jsonld"</span>,
    <span class="tok-str">"https://sockethub.org/ns/context/platform/whatsapp/v1.jsonld"</span>
  ],
  <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>:   <span class="tok-str">"credentials"</span>,
  <span class="tok-key">"actor"</span>:  { <span class="tok-key">"id"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"&lt;phone number id&gt;"</span>, <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"person"</span> },
  <span class="tok-key">"object"</span>: {
    <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>:       <span class="tok-str">"credentials"</span>,
    <span class="tok-key">"token"</span>:      <span class="tok-str">"…"</span>,
    <span class="tok-key">"apiVersion"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"v22.0"</span>
  }
}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Create a Meta developer app with the WhatsApp use case and register
          a business phone number. <code>actor.id</code> is its phone number
          ID from Meta, and the access token needs
          <code>whatsapp_business_messaging</code>. Choose an API version
          supported by your Meta app.
        </p>

        <h3 class="protocol__section">2. Send a text message</h3>
        <pre class="envelope-block"><code>{
  <span class="tok-key">"@context"</span>: [ <span class="tok-comment">/* as above */</span> ],
  <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>:   <span class="tok-str">"send"</span>,
  <span class="tok-key">"actor"</span>:  { <span class="tok-key">"id"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"&lt;phone number id&gt;"</span>, <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"person"</span> },
  <span class="tok-key">"target"</span>: { <span class="tok-key">"id"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"+15551234567"</span>,         <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"person"</span> },
  <span class="tok-key">"object"</span>: { <span class="tok-key">"type"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"message"</span>, <span class="tok-key">"content"</span>: <span class="tok-str">"Hello from Sockethub!"</span> }
}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Use the recipient's international phone number. The platform adds
          a leading plus sign when one is missing. Messages are text only,
          up to 4096 characters. Meta accepts free-form text only within
          24 hours of the recipient's last message; template messages are
          not supported. A successful acknowledgement includes Meta's
          message ID and confirms API acceptance, not delivery. Incoming
          messages, receipts, media, and webhook hosting are outside this
          platform.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

